    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/1510.09011v1</id>
    <title>A Provably Stable Discontinuous Galerkin Spectral Element Approximation for Moving Hexahedral Meshes</title>
    <updated>2015-10-30T09:00:28Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1510.09011v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/1510.09011v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>We design a novel provably stable discontinuous Galerkin spectral element (DGSEM) approximation to solve systems of conservation laws on moving domains. To incorporate the motion of the domain, we use an arbitrary Lagrangian-Eulerian formulation to map the governing equations to a fixed reference domain. The approximation is made stable by a discretization of a skew-symmetric formulation of the problem. We prove that the discrete approximation is stable, conservative and, for constant coefficient problems, maintains the free-stream preservation property. We also provide details on how to add the new skew-symmetric ALE approximation to an existing discontinuous Galerkin spectral element code. Lastly, we provide numerical support of the theoretical results.</summary>
