    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/1207.4219v2</id>
    <title>Radio Labelings of Distance Graphs</title>
    <updated>2013-03-18T14:01:05Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1207.4219v2" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/1207.4219v2" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>A radio $k$-labeling of a connected graph $G$ is an assignment $c$ of non negative integers to the vertices of $G$ such that $$|c(x) - c(y)| \geq k+1 - d(x,y),$$ for any two vertices $x$ and $y$, $x\ne y$, where $d(x,y)$ is the distance between $x$ and $y$ in $G$. In this paper, we study radio labelings of distance graphs, i.e., graphs with the set $\Z$ of integers as vertex set and in which two distinct vertices $i, j \in \Z$ are adjacent if and only if $|i - j| \in D$.</summary>
